[{"data":1,"prerenderedAt":305},["ShallowReactive",2],{"news:\u002Fnews\u002F2011-07-29-updating-old-lunar-installations-getting-rid-of-hal":3,"news-timeline":86},{"id":4,"title":5,"author":6,"body":7,"date":76,"description":77,"extension":78,"meta":79,"navigation":80,"path":81,"readingTime":82,"seo":83,"stem":84,"__hash__":85},"news\u002Fnews\u002F2011-07-29-updating-old-lunar-installations-getting-rid-of-hal.md","Updating old lunar installations: Getting rid of hal","wdp",{"type":8,"value":9,"toc":73},"minimark",[10,14,25,50,61,67],[11,12,13],"p",{},"As hal is deprecated now, most new-installations don’t have it anymore. My netbook still has it, so how do I get rid of it easily? Read on, if you want to know..",[15,16,21],"pre",{"className":17,"code":19,"language":20},[18],"language-text","lrm hal-info hal\nfor i in `lsh list_installed_depending hal`; do lin -cr \"$i\"; done\nlunar fixdepends\nlunar fix\n","text",[22,23,19],"code",{"__ignoreMap":24},"",[11,26,27,30,31,34,35,38,39,42,43,45,46,49],{},[22,28,29],{},"lunar fixdepends"," might not be needed; however. Basically I’m removing ",[22,32,33],{},"hal-info"," and ",[22,36,37],{},"hal",". Then I’m going through all modules which have hal as dependency and I’m relinning them using ",[22,40,41],{},"lin -cr"," (which will ask me everything again so I can say no to hal). Right after doing so, I’m running ",[22,44,29],{}," to re-create the dependency stuff and ",[22,47,48],{},"lunar fix"," to resolve any other issues which might be there due to the removal of hal.",[11,51,52,56,57,60],{},[53,54,55],"strong",{},"lsh"," is lunar’s internal .. well. let’s name it “lunar shell” which is just a shell with lunar functions. Those functions you’ll find in ",[22,58,59],{},"\u002Fvar\u002Flib\u002Flunar\u002Ffunctions\u002F",". You can use them for quite useful stuff.",[11,62,63,66],{},[53,64,65],{},"Note"," for correct “dependency” order it would be better to have the dependencies in “one” line instead of doing that “for”. I.e.:",[15,68,71],{"className":69,"code":70,"language":20},[18],"MODULES=\"\"; for i in `lsh list_installed_depending hal`; do   VAR=$(echo \"$MODULES\" | grep \"$i\"); if [ -z \"$VAR\" ]; then      MODULES=\"$MODULES $i\";   fi; done\n",[22,72,70],{"__ignoreMap":24},{"title":24,"searchDepth":74,"depth":74,"links":75},3,[],"2011-07-29","How to remove the deprecated hal from an older installation and rebuild what depended on it.","md",{},true,"\u002Fnews\u002F2011-07-29-updating-old-lunar-installations-getting-rid-of-hal",2,{"title":5,"description":77},"news\u002F2011-07-29-updating-old-lunar-installations-getting-rid-of-hal","d2twRMd5qwIZZ12WKLB2OB-OWXgT7sLS5SfK50_Mk7w",[87,91,95,99,103,107,111,115,119,123,127,131,134,138,142,146,150,153,157,161,162,166,170,174,178,182,186,190,194,198,202,206,210,214,218,222,226,230,234,238,242,246,250,254,258,262,266,270,274,278,282,286,290,294,297,301],{"title":88,"path":89,"date":90},"Moving towards a more aggressive release cycle","\u002Fnews\u002F2023-08-13-moving-towards-a-more-aggressive-release-cycle","2023-08-13",{"title":92,"path":93,"date":94},"We are moving to libera.chat network","\u002Fnews\u002F2021-05-23-we-are-moving-to-libera-chat-network","2021-05-23",{"title":96,"path":97,"date":98},"We are still very much alive","\u002Fnews\u002F2017-10-18-we-are-still-very-much-alive","2017-10-18",{"title":100,"path":101,"date":102},"Lunar Linux 1.7.0 (i686 & x86_64) ISO’s released","\u002Fnews\u002F2014-10-11-lunar-linux-1-7-0-i686-and-x86-64-isos-released","2014-10-11",{"title":104,"path":105,"date":106},"Lunar Linux 1.7.0-rc2 (i686 & x86_64) ISO’s released","\u002Fnews\u002F2014-09-16-lunar-linux-1-7-0-rc2-i686-and-x86-64-isos-released","2014-09-16",{"title":108,"path":109,"date":110},"Service transition","\u002Fnews\u002F2014-05-24-service-transition","2014-05-24",{"title":112,"path":113,"date":114},"Services from lunar-linux.org may be disrupted","\u002Fnews\u002F2014-05-19-services-from-lunar-linux-org-may-be-disrupted","20